00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.330
Nicole: Ethical conduct refers to
standards of behaviour that are

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:07.300
appropriate and shows understanding
of what is right and what is wrong.

00:00:08.429 --> 00:00:12.600
Abraham: In cyber security unlike
other industries there is no specific

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:16.580
code of ethics though many employers
and organisations will have their own

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:20.779
codes of conduct or ethics covering
other aspects of their organisations,

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:24.290
as well as security that need to
be complied with by all staff.

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:29.449
Nicole: It is also very important that
all organisations that handle data do

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:34.339
so in an ethical way to make sure that
they abide by legislation and regulations

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:38.460
that we have already looked at relating
to the use of computers and data.

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:42.680
Abraham: All organisations and
companies will have an IT policy

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:46.980
in place, and some will also have
a specific cyber security policy.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:51.010
These will be regularly reviewed
and updated to keep in touch with

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:53.220
ever changing laws and regulations.

00:00:53.489 --> 00:00:57.490
Nicole: Most new employees must sign
up to a policy agreement as part

00:00:57.490 --> 00:01:01.600
of their induction to say that they
will follow all guidelines including

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:06.250
ethical ones especially where specific
sensitive data is concerned and

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:08.059
GDPR rules need to be adhered to.

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:12.919
There are a range of ethical rules that
link to legislation when it comes to

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:15.660
using computer systems that apply such as:

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:18.450
• Abraham: Not using computer
equipment to harm others.

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:22.130
• Not interfering with
other’s computers and work

00:01:22.719 --> 00:01:25.540
• Not looking through other’s
files without their permission.

00:01:26.059 --> 00:01:29.409
• Not using a computer to
steal or cause mischief.

00:01:29.879 --> 00:01:31.229
• Not copying software.

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:34.670
• Not using other people’s
resources without permission.

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:37.580
• Acting without regard for consequences.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:40.650
• And having respect for data security.

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:45.509
Nicole: With remote working, more
employees work from home, but, all

00:01:45.509 --> 00:01:47.429
of these rules should still apply.

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:52.100
And remember ethical conduct goes
both ways employees may sync their

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:56.850
work emails to their smartphones, and
employers may come to expect workers

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:59.270
to check emails outside office hours.

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:04.439
Abraham: It is not ethical of a business
to expect employees to be available at all

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:06.580
hours unless this is part of their role.

